1
00:00:01,500 --> 00:00:03,279
Azure changes every day.

2
00:00:03,700 --> 00:00:05,279
Most of it has nothing to do with you.

3
00:00:07,800 --> 00:00:11,379
But somewhere in that noise is the
one that takes down production.

4
00:00:13,200 --> 00:00:17,001
And the alerts meant to protect
you? Switched on everywhere.

5
00:00:17,001 --> 00:00:18,129
Quietly ignored.

6
00:00:19,800 --> 00:00:23,179
The problem was never
signal. It's context.

7
00:00:24,100 --> 00:00:26,029
This is CloudLens.

8
00:00:26,300 --> 00:00:31,729
It listens to Azure Updates, Microsoft
Learn, and Azure Service Health.

9
00:00:31,979 --> 00:00:37,544
AI analyzes every item for severity,
deadline, and migration path.

10
00:00:37,794 --> 00:00:42,073
Then it asks the only question that
matters: does this touch my estate?

11
00:00:43,000 --> 00:00:45,279
Context starts with
knowing what's production.

12
00:00:45,800 --> 00:00:48,906
It ranks your subscriptions
by spend, production tags

13
00:00:48,906 --> 00:00:52,129
and live workload signals,
in an order you control.

14
00:00:53,400 --> 00:00:56,350
So alerts go only where action is likely.

15
00:00:56,350 --> 00:00:59,229
Not everywhere. Where it matters.

16
00:01:00,000 --> 00:01:04,329
Then AI adds the context,
and noise becomes signal.

17
00:01:04,700 --> 00:01:06,738
Not "this service is retiring.

18
00:01:06,738 --> 00:01:09,794
" But: seven of your
production clusters,

19
00:01:09,794 --> 00:01:12,579
across four regions, in one subscription.

20
00:01:12,829 --> 00:01:16,257
What to do, who owns
it, and by when.

21
00:01:17,000 --> 00:01:19,579
That's not a headline.
That's a work item.

22
00:01:21,100 --> 00:01:24,779
Every deadline tracked. 
Every delivery confirmed.

23
00:01:25,029 --> 00:01:27,107
And it lands where your
teams already work.

24
00:01:28,200 --> 00:01:31,337
The Teams channel that
owns it. Your wiki.

25
00:01:31,337 --> 00:01:33,929
A work item, or a GitHub issue.

26
00:01:35,500 --> 00:01:38,029
Ticketing tools like
ServiceNow can connect, too.

27
00:01:39,100 --> 00:01:41,929
Zero keys. Private by design.

28
00:01:42,200 --> 00:01:46,129
Less noise. More
context. Faster action.

29
00:01:46,379 --> 00:01:49,907
CloudLens. From radar to response.
